    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change was contained entirely to `AssignCustomerCode.service`, the single function that builds `customerCode`.\n\n- **Format**: `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2192 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `CITY3` is the upper-cased first three letters of the city, `LAST3` the first three of the last name.\n- **Sequence**: was a global count (`findAll().size() + 1`); now a per-city count \u2014 one more than the owners already in that same city (case-insensitive), still excluding the owner being created since assignment runs pre-save.\n- **Derived values**: the membership number in `OwnerMapper` is `customerCode + \"-M\" + <year>`, so it rebuilds on the new format automatically with no edit needed.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: only one file and one method changed. I extracted the repeated three-letter prefix logic into a tiny private static helper (`three`) so `service` stays simple (its city/last-name prefixing collapses to two calls), rather than inlining and growing the method's complexity.",
